## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/file.html
- Summary (EN): The File node brings image or video files from disk into a COP network. It can also import the AOVs and their properties from a source file, which then become the node's outputs.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud File charge une image ou une vidéo depuis le disque dans le réseau COP, avec ses AOV et ses métadonnées.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output image size and controls the metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Source: File on disk, Clone from the Clone Control Panel, or Live Render LOP", "File Name: path to an image, image sequence or video; tokens $F or <F> for sequence frames, <UDIM> for UDIM tiles, <LAYER> for multiple AOV files", "Video Timing: frame numbers generated from a Start Frame or a specific Frame Number", "Border: raster edge handling (Default, Constant, Clamp, Mirror, Wrap) when Tile Visualization is on", "Missing Data: report an error or warning, or substitute a Missing Color, for missing AOVs or frames", "Incoming Colorspace: interprets color via OpenColorIO rules, as raw data, or with pre-multiplication where needed", "Load Camera: reads camera data from file metadata to set the layer transform and camera", "Display Window from Input: uses the input's display window so pixels correspond one-to-one", "Add AOVs from File: imports AOVs from the file; Ctrl+click resets the list", "Number of AOVs, File AOV, Channel Type, Precision, Raw: source name, data format (Mono, UV, RGB, RGBA, ID), bit depth and color handling of each loaded AOV"]

- Caveats: ["Several parameters override the defaults set on the enclosing COP Network node or COP Network SOP", "Video files only support the C AOV"]

